  <sharedRules>
    <rule name="Sewer Sherpas" id="014d-9344-2dde-c2a4" hidden="false">
      <description>Once per Player Turn, a Sewer move may be declared for a Single Infantry unit under the Controlling Player&apos;s control. For a Sewer Move to be considered eligible, the Controlling Player must select One Objective marker on the board, and that Objective Marker must follow both of the following criteria.


- That Objective Marker was under the Control of the Controlling Player at the end of the previous player turn


- That Objective Marker is not contested


To perform a Sewer Move, during the Move Subphase, the Controlling Player must select One Infantry unit that has not yet made a move this turn. The Controlling Player&apos;s unit is considered to have the Antigrav Subtype until the Sewer Move is resolved, and the Movement Characteristic of all Models in that Unit is set to the distance between that Unit&apos;s current position and the selected Objective Marker. The Infantry unit must then move as close as possible to that Objective Marker.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
